WEBVTT

00:02.250 --> 00:03.960
The Castle H Ruins, Danger Rank S!

00:12.540 --> 00:14.750
Something feels wrong.

01:55.290 --> 01:57.790
You look delicious.

01:58.210 --> 02:03.580
No clue why you're carryin' this scrumptious thing,
but thank ya kindly.

02:10.540 --> 02:13.170
She moved? How?!

02:13.380 --> 02:16.250
The illusion should still be controlling her!

02:16.790 --> 02:20.330
She's still unconscious...

02:20.960 --> 02:23.420
Her finger's movin' on its own!

02:24.380 --> 02:25.420
No!

02:28.130 --> 02:30.290
YAYOI-CHAN!

02:33.920 --> 02:35.130
Keitaro?

03:06.580 --> 03:08.290
I got you, Grandma.

03:11.670 --> 03:14.460
If I hadn't heard Keitaro's voice, I might not have made it.

03:15.130 --> 03:19.380
This spirit saved my butt, too.

03:20.250 --> 03:24.250
Not that it had any choice,
since if she'd attacked me, it would've gotten hurt.

03:24.960 --> 03:27.210
It was just acting in self-defense.

03:28.130 --> 03:29.330
Still...

03:30.080 --> 03:33.960
Thank you, both of you.

03:36.710 --> 03:40.080
Keitaro's probably still in trouble. I'd better hurry.

03:46.460 --> 03:48.330
Yayoi-chan...

03:50.170 --> 03:53.460
It's over. It's hopeless.

03:58.500 --> 03:59.920
Got you!

04:00.830 --> 04:01.670
It's the ghost!

04:02.460 --> 04:04.540
Let go of me!

04:05.000 --> 04:09.080
But there's one thing I know
from this shitty turn of events...

04:09.670 --> 04:13.580
Yayoi-chan is still alive!
The hanging corpse wasn't her at all!

04:14.330 --> 04:16.960
And if she's alive, she's definitely gonna catch this thing!

04:17.250 --> 04:19.330
No more freaking out about it!

04:28.170 --> 04:30.500
It's getting pulled up into the sky?

04:32.170 --> 04:35.580
Wait, something's embedded in that dome...

04:37.250 --> 04:38.420
Skeletons?

04:39.500 --> 04:40.960
And they're wearing modern clothing.

04:41.420 --> 04:44.670
Is that what happened to the people
who came here looking for ghosts?

04:44.670 --> 04:46.500
I'll hold you here...

04:47.170 --> 04:48.790
...until that wound...

04:49.830 --> 04:52.080
...severs your head from your neck.

04:52.670 --> 04:57.000
Then I'll keep you here long after you're dead,

04:58.170 --> 05:00.130
so you can join them.

05:01.330 --> 05:06.000
She must be talking about the skeletons up in the dome.

05:06.790 --> 05:09.750
Is that what's gonna happen to me?!

05:13.380 --> 05:14.170
Not happening.

05:30.210 --> 05:31.290
Yayoi-chan!

05:31.750 --> 05:33.380
You okay, Keitaro?

05:33.580 --> 05:37.960
Y-you're okay! Thank God, you're okay!

05:37.960 --> 05:40.000
Keitaro, keep your guard up.

05:44.580 --> 05:49.460
Yayoi-chan, this spirit casts a curse
that slowly slices through your neck.

05:50.540 --> 05:54.710
The dome over us is made from a huge number of spirits,
which are all part of the main one.

05:55.290 --> 06:02.250
It traps its target to keep them from escaping,
then waits for the curse to decapitate them.

06:03.880 --> 06:07.000
But even after they're dead, it won't let them go.

06:07.540 --> 06:13.080
It must be consuming the souls of those it kills
to get even stronger.

06:13.670 --> 06:15.960
That's what I've been able to put together!

06:16.500 --> 06:19.960
And I'm guessing the reason
we haven't heard of anyone dying here

06:20.670 --> 06:26.210
is because anyone who's encountered this spirit
has never survived to tell the tale.

06:27.420 --> 06:29.000
It's ridiculously powerful.

06:29.540 --> 06:30.420
Mm-hmm.

06:31.380 --> 06:32.460
It's scared.

06:33.500 --> 06:36.250
Almost like it wants to back up Keitaro's theory.

06:37.500 --> 06:40.580
Let's get started, then. Can you put me down?

06:41.250 --> 06:42.500
Shoot, sorry!

06:43.710 --> 06:48.380
H..hold on, Yayoi-chan,
how do we even deal with a spirit this strong?

06:48.880 --> 06:51.790
I don't know if anything I said just now even helped.

06:51.960 --> 06:53.330
It's simple.

06:53.750 --> 06:55.000
We bring in a pinch hitter...

06:59.040 --> 07:02.960
...and overwhelm it with our own powerful blow.

07:06.170 --> 07:07.170
Begin your sermon,

07:08.250 --> 07:10.000
High Priest of the Evil Tongue.

07:24.540 --> 07:25.580
A sutra?!

07:26.670 --> 07:27.540
Keitaro.

07:28.130 --> 07:29.790
These are noise-cancelling headphones.

07:30.670 --> 07:35.420
Blast music in your ears.
Don't let yourself hear the sutra at all.

07:44.920 --> 07:46.710
It'll end you.

07:47.420 --> 07:50.830
Is this what I was gonna hear?!

08:11.790 --> 08:15.960
It's pulling the female ghosts out from the huge spirit...

08:16.790 --> 08:21.790
Anyone who hears this sutra, dead or alive,
is forced to pass on to the afterlife.

08:22.710 --> 08:24.250
But all of them will go...

08:25.040 --> 08:26.210
...straight to Hell.

08:58.580 --> 09:00.040
It stopped the sutra.

09:40.750 --> 09:44.670
It's breaking apart the huge spirit...

10:17.290 --> 10:18.080
It's escaping!

10:18.290 --> 10:19.790
No, it's not.

10:20.580 --> 10:25.250
It's trying to buy itself time by killing
all the living beings who could speak the sutra.

10:26.580 --> 10:27.420
Yayoi-chan!

10:27.670 --> 10:31.540
If we lose our only weapon, it'll devour the Graduate.

10:31.960 --> 10:33.290
We can't let it out of our sight!

10:37.380 --> 10:40.540
It's gone. It's too dark to see.

10:43.250 --> 10:44.210
It's this way!

10:46.000 --> 10:52.210
Now that the huge spirit's gone,
I can use my spiritual sense to feel where it is!

11:00.460 --> 11:02.130
It's not covering its ears.

11:02.420 --> 11:04.750
Does that mean it can't hear the sutra?

11:05.380 --> 11:06.210
That's not good!

11:28.540 --> 11:30.790
This is the end.

11:34.790 --> 11:40.040
To think I would feel this despair even in death...

11:43.920 --> 11:47.500
Pick your poison. Stay, or disappear.

11:53.000 --> 11:56.040
The Castle H Ruins ghost is mine.

11:58.830 --> 12:02.880
We did it, Yayoi-chan. Let's go home.

12:28.080 --> 12:35.830
The High Priest of the Evil Tongue
chants a sutra that drags its listeners to Hell.

12:36.380 --> 12:41.630
And now, against my will,
my mouth is chanting that sutra!

12:53.250 --> 12:58.500
I pressed my hand in his mouth
to stimulate his gag reflex and stop him from talking.

12:59.250 --> 13:02.380
In that position, I can also
spiritually attack part of his mind.

13:02.750 --> 13:06.210
The attack will harm the dolls that have Keitaro's nail in it,

13:06.710 --> 13:09.750
hurting the same part I'm attacking on Keitaro,

13:10.880 --> 13:12.790
and knocking out the Priest!

13:15.540 --> 13:16.380
It stopped.

13:16.880 --> 13:21.500
With the Priest passed out, it can't chant, so no evil sutra.

13:21.960 --> 13:24.210
Thank God it didn't resist, though.

13:24.880 --> 13:27.920
Keitaro, you have to seal the High Priest, now!

13:29.210 --> 13:33.540
Looks like it takes two to three seconds
to kill a small animal,

13:34.250 --> 13:36.290
and ten seconds for bigger animals!

13:37.880 --> 13:43.540
I bet most humans can only take it for twenty seconds.
That's how long you have to seal it!

13:44.460 --> 13:48.460
I'll attack him to buy more time!

13:48.880 --> 13:50.790
You seal up the doll!

13:52.250 --> 13:56.380
Are you kidding?! I've never sealed anything,
and you want me to do it like this?!

14:00.580 --> 14:01.460
Hurry!

14:03.380 --> 14:05.710
Screw it, let's go!

14:07.290 --> 14:08.210
It stopped.

14:09.380 --> 14:10.580
But it recovers too quick!

14:12.630 --> 14:13.500
I'll try again!

14:17.580 --> 14:18.460
It resisted!

14:20.830 --> 14:21.540
Hang in there!

14:27.380 --> 14:28.290
It stopped.

14:32.500 --> 14:35.750
One second slower, and we both would've been goners.

14:36.460 --> 14:40.000
Y-you didn't have to take out your headphones.

14:40.960 --> 14:42.420
We're in this together.

14:44.830 --> 14:46.210
Good work, partner.

14:48.790 --> 14:50.460
That should wrap things up nicely.

14:56.830 --> 14:59.420
There's a weird aura connected to the doll.

15:00.210 --> 15:01.380
Let's check it out.

15:01.380 --> 15:02.960
Hold up, Yayoi-chan!

15:07.170 --> 15:09.130
We're back at the waterfall.

15:12.540 --> 15:15.210
There's something over there.

15:20.540 --> 15:21.540
Yayoi-chan?

15:24.670 --> 15:26.920
<b>CURSE</b>

15:24.670 --> 15:26.920
<b>SEALED</b>

15:25.420 --> 15:27.630
Wait, a box?

15:28.210 --> 15:29.210
Let's see what's inside.

15:34.960 --> 15:35.920
A talisman.

15:36.290 --> 15:38.330
What the hell is that?

15:55.710 --> 15:57.960
Betting this caused you lots of trouble.

15:59.210 --> 16:02.540
The anger and hatred drove me mad...

16:04.250 --> 16:07.880
Keitaro, I was right.
The ghost of these ruins isn't an evil spirit.

16:07.880 --> 16:08.580
Huh?

16:08.960 --> 16:15.710
It was just a powerful spirit,
driven mad by this evil talisman.

16:16.500 --> 16:19.670
Getting rid of it brought her back to normal.

16:20.460 --> 16:22.130
Come to think of it,

16:22.750 --> 16:27.210
it acted like it was trying to share its memories
of the castle ruins.

16:27.750 --> 16:33.750
But because of this talisman,
it killed people to make them a part of it.

16:34.330 --> 16:38.040
That contradicts with its goal
of sharing memories with the living.

16:38.670 --> 16:40.830
The madness must have driven them to it.

16:42.130 --> 16:48.330
Wait, then doesn't that mean we sent a whole bunch
of good spirits straight to Hell?!

16:48.330 --> 16:51.670
Not quite. You've got the wrong idea.

16:52.170 --> 16:56.290
There weren't multiple spirits here.

16:56.670 --> 17:00.040
Then what was that? Because I saw tons of spirits.

17:00.380 --> 17:02.580
Multiple spirits can't fuse into one.

17:02.960 --> 17:05.380
That makes this a split spirit.

17:05.750 --> 17:06.880
"A split spirit"?

17:07.170 --> 17:09.920
You know how one god's soul
might be split into multiple parts,

17:10.210 --> 17:16.500
then spread out through a bunch of shrines
to be worshipped? It's the same deal.

17:12.290 --> 17:14.500
<b>One god's spirit</b>

17:12.290 --> 17:14.500
<b>Split Spirit</b>

17:17.330 --> 17:18.290
Am I right?

17:20.790 --> 17:25.040
I split my soul to recreate my memories,

17:26.500 --> 17:32.960
so that the gentle and proud people
who once lived here would never be forgotten...

17:34.250 --> 17:38.880
The spirits sent to Hell can't fuse back with their source,
so they just disappear.

17:39.580 --> 17:44.210
To address your first comment,
we didn't send anyone to Hell.

17:44.540 --> 17:46.960
We just weakened the main spirit.

17:48.040 --> 17:54.790
But this location is powerful in itself.
She'll regain her power without consuming spirits.

17:55.670 --> 17:59.630
No matter the reason, you still killed people.

18:00.130 --> 18:02.830
So that weakening is your punishment for murder.

18:03.540 --> 18:06.830
I'll never forget what you've done to me.

18:07.210 --> 18:09.130
We know. That won't stop us.

18:09.630 --> 18:12.080
Still, I don't want you to be too weak.

18:21.380 --> 18:22.380
There she goes.

18:22.580 --> 18:24.040
Then she wasn't part of the spirit?

18:24.580 --> 18:27.130
She was probably just a wandering ghost
that got roped into things.

18:27.630 --> 18:30.080
Leave her be, and she'll eventually pass on.

18:30.580 --> 18:32.630
Our biggest problem is this talisman.

18:33.000 --> 18:35.920
Someone must have known about the spirit
and placed the talisman here,

18:36.420 --> 18:38.670
with the sole purpose of driving the spirit mad.

18:39.380 --> 18:40.460
This was deliberate.

18:42.630 --> 18:46.420
Let's bury it somewhere else so this won't happen again.

18:47.210 --> 18:50.460
Fortunately, since I captured her,
she's not bound here anymore.

18:56.750 --> 18:58.380
Okay, that looks good.

18:59.290 --> 19:00.790
Now we just gotta bury it.

19:00.790 --> 19:04.000
All this digging late at night
makes me feel like we're hiding a corpse...

19:04.290 --> 19:07.670
This should put an end to the ghost stories here.

19:08.170 --> 19:10.290
Bet this place will get loads of tourism.

19:12.170 --> 19:13.250
Keitaro.

19:13.960 --> 19:20.540
If you hadn't called out for me,
or used your spirit sense, I would've ended up dead.

19:21.380 --> 19:22.420
Thanks.

19:22.830 --> 19:26.330
Wow. I'm just glad I helped out a little.

19:28.790 --> 19:32.880
But thank you. You saved me, too.

19:34.790 --> 19:38.830
I was really scared. I seriously thought we were done for.

19:39.290 --> 19:42.460
I thought the two of us were totally dead.

19:43.080 --> 19:46.210
Honestly, I'm kinda surprised we actually survived.

19:47.420 --> 19:48.380
Keitaro.

19:48.630 --> 19:50.500
Do you want to stop ghost hunting?

19:55.960 --> 19:58.040
I'll be honest, I'm terrified.

19:58.540 --> 20:04.920
When we got separated,
when that ghost made me think you were dead...

20:05.500 --> 20:08.130
I screamed and cried like a little kid.

20:09.290 --> 20:11.790
But that made me realize,

20:12.500 --> 20:20.290
I was only so upset about losing you
because I care about you so much.

20:22.040 --> 20:24.540
I'm not giving up on ghost hunting yet.

20:25.540 --> 20:28.710
I mean, you're not gonna stop anytime soon, right?

20:30.080 --> 20:34.710
Then, I'll push through my fear to be
by your side and help out however I can.

20:35.670 --> 20:37.540
To make sure I never lose you.

20:43.880 --> 20:45.330
That does it!

20:47.080 --> 20:48.670
Okay, let's go home!

20:49.000 --> 20:49.540
Yeah.

20:53.540 --> 20:57.290
Keitaro, if you're ever in the dark,

20:58.080 --> 21:00.380
remember how this feels.

21:03.880 --> 21:08.130
I'll sear it into my memory... And my heart.

21:23.710 --> 21:25.750
I won't forget what you've done to me.

21:26.630 --> 21:29.710
And what you've done for me.

21:31.580 --> 21:33.250
Call upon me if you need help.

21:33.500 --> 21:34.290
Same goes for you.

21:45.250 --> 21:52.580
With that, our first night handling
an S-Rank haunt came to an end.

21:54.880 --> 21:56.630
Harrumph...

21:55.500 --> 21:56.750
<b>HA-                                                           -RRUMPH</b>

21:56.920 --> 21:58.420
You ditched me!

21:58.420 --> 22:01.670
S-sorry! It all happened so quickly!

22:02.170 --> 22:04.460
C'mon, Yayoi-chan, say you're sorry!

22:04.960 --> 22:06.580
It was so scary.

22:06.580 --> 22:11.290
Sorry you had to do homework and couldn't go,
because it was mega scary.

22:12.880 --> 22:13.540
Spill the deets!

22:13.540 --> 22:14.420
I should've figured!

22:16.170 --> 22:18.500
That basically covers the whole story.

22:19.630 --> 22:23.420
Let me ask you a question
that will hopefully make it up to you.

22:24.040 --> 22:26.790
Do you want to go somewhere even scarier?

22:28.080 --> 22:29.380
Hold up, Yayoi-chan!

22:29.380 --> 22:32.290
Castle H was dangerous enough, and you wanna-

22:32.290 --> 22:32.830
Cause we can.

22:33.670 --> 22:36.040
I know how strong the High Priest is now,

22:36.580 --> 22:39.380
and we've got the Castle H spirit helping, too.

22:40.540 --> 22:43.880
We can use her split spirits as shields if need be.

22:45.580 --> 22:48.710
After all that work to get the castle ghost to help us,

22:48.710 --> 22:49.920
you're just gonna ruin it?!

22:50.330 --> 22:52.670
Okay, where are we headed?!

22:53.250 --> 22:57.790
The sealed-off haunt that's known
for sightings of a woman in a kimono,

22:58.290 --> 23:06.250
<b>Danger: S</b>

22:58.290 --> 23:06.250
<b>Woman in a white kimono</b>

22:58.290 --> 23:06.500
<b>O City: Old F Tunnel</b>

22:58.290 --> 23:06.500
<b>Danger: S</b>

22:58.300 --> 23:06.500
<b>O City</b>

22:58.670 --> 23:01.710
the sound of crying from beyond the blockade,

23:02.420 --> 23:06.500
and a sense of something creepy coming closer.

23:07.380 --> 23:09.960
O City in Tokyo, the Old F Tunnel.

23:11.170 --> 23:14.750
We're finally headed to a place
every supernatural geek knows by heart!

23:14.790 --> 23:17.330
<b>O City: Old F Tunnel</b>

23:14.790 --> 23:17.330
<b>Danger: S</b>

23:15.710 --> 23:19.960
Not another Rank S...

23:22.290 --> 23:29.920
As Yayoi and the gang prep to head
to another S-Rank haunt to add to their growing army,

23:30.210 --> 23:32.630
they seek out another Graduate.

23:34.080 --> 23:39.130
But two dark clouds threaten to obstruct their path...
